  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Heat is produced at a rate given by $H$ in a resistor when it is connected across a supply of voltage $V$. If now the resistance of the resistor is doubled and the supply voltage is made $V / 3$, then the rate of production of heat in the resistor will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "L07DZ",
      "text": "$H / 18$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9xS0d",
      "text": "$H / 9$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9l2mb",
      "text": "$6 \\mathrm{H}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wGYKg",
      "text": "$18 H$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know $H=\\frac{V^{2}}{R}$ Here, in second condition $V$ becomes $\\frac{V}{3}$ and $R^{\\prime}$ becomes $2 R$.\r\nSo,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nH^{\\prime}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{V}{3}\\right)^{2}}{2 R}=\\frac{V^{2}}{18 R} \\\\\r\nH^{\\prime}=\\frac{H}{18}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
